The matrix is a discovery tool, not a finding of bribery.

XXIV. Potential predicate offenses

Dismissal of a civil case is not a RICO predicate.

Potential predicate conduct could arise if evidence establishes:
Federal or state bribery;

Honest-services wire fraud based on bribery or kickbacks;

Wire fraud through concealed payment arrangements or false conflict disclosures;

Money laundering involving payments for official action;

Obstruction of justice;

Destruction or concealment of enforcement records;
Witness tampering;
