DOGE-14 — World Liberty Financial, USD1, Binance, UAE Capital, and the Alleged Monetization of Presidential Authority

I. Investigative purpose

This exhibit examines whether World Liberty Financial and its USD1 stablecoin became a mechanism through which domestic or foreign interests could confer substantial financial benefits on businesses associated with President Donald J. Trump while seeking favorable governmental action.

The investigation focuses on whether connections among World Liberty Financial, the Trump family, the Witkoff family, MGX, Binance, the United Arab Emirates, federal digital-asset policy, enforcement dismissals, technology agreements, and executive clemency demonstrate:

an unprecedented but lawful presidential conflict of interest;
regulatory capture and preferential access;
monetization of presidential status without an explicit exchange;
concealed foreign influence;
bribery or another corrupt exchange of private value for official action; or
participation in a broader racketeering enterprise.

No criminal conclusion should be reached without proof connecting a particular financial benefit to a particular official act or governmental course of action.

II. Principal persons and entities

Potential subjects, witnesses, and record custodians include:

Donald J. Trump;
Eric Trump, Donald Trump Jr., and other relevant Trump-family representatives;
the Donald J. Trump Revocable Trust and affiliated entities;
