White House digital-asset policy personnel;
DOGE officials;
congressional and executive-branch ethics officials; and
foreign token purchasers, exchanges, market makers, and beneficial owners.

Identification does not imply criminal participation.

III. Core theory of monetization

The alleged monetization structure differs from an ordinary campaign contribution.

A foreign or domestic party could potentially provide economic value by:

purchasing WLFI tokens;
using USD1 in a large transaction;
holding USD1 for an extended period;
providing liquidity;
listing USD1 on an exchange;
selecting USD1 as collateral;
integrating USD1 into another blockchain;
acquiring an interest in World Liberty Financial;
increasing the venture’s visibility and credibility; or
creating demand that generates reserve interest and commercial fees.

If a purchaser expected no official action, the transaction may be a legitimate commercial investment.

If value was provided pursuant to an understanding that the President or administration would take favorable governmental action, the same transaction could become evidence of corruption.

IV. World Liberty Financial’s connection to President Trump

President Trump’s 2025 public financial disclosure reported interests associated with World Liberty Financial, including:

15.75 billion World Liberty Financial governance tokens;
